  "material_note": "painted_steel rather than plate_steel, and the reason is measurable: steel.jpg averages 0.083 in linear where iron's reflectance is 0.56. It is a painting of a lit blade, not a measurement of one, and handed to a renderer as metal it came back as black chrome.\n\nThe tools became brass, decided on the bench and against the note above. That note argued painted_steel over plate_steel because steel.jpg is a painting of a lit blade averaging 0.083 in linear, and handed to a renderer as metal it came back as black chrome. It is not the sheet any more: the tools now wear a photoscan, whose albedo is a measurement rather than a painted highlight, and metal is written into the ORM's blue at 1.0 rather than left to a factor that had nothing to multiply.",
